  {
    "sha": "c3efcfe7cbb0fec19cfb8849aeadde05fa954f99",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGMzZWZjZmU3Y2JiMGZlYzE5Y2ZiODg0OWFlYWRkZTA1ZmE5NTRmOTk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T18:11:47Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T18:11:47Z"
      },
      "message": "perf(sim): walk the operation starts one time for each timeline\n\nReview of PR #2763. The step buttons called the Script lookups in each\nframe, and each call walked every segment of the timeline. OpStarts::of\nnow walks the segments one time; next, prev and op_at are binary\nsearches over one entry for each operation. The transport keeps the\nstarts in State beside the cached script, keyed on the script's Arc\n(sim_steps::cached_op_starts).\n\nA new test pins the value of each start from the segments, and a UI\ntest pins that a still frame walks no segment. The Gate map line of\nsim_op_step_stock names camcraft_sim::sim.\n\nRefs #2608\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
