  {
    "sha": "7cdb8b8d94a8329ad250bc4853ec5a6ea4f6891f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDdjZGI4YjhkOTRhODMyOWFkMjUwYmM0ODUzZWM1YTZlYTRmNjg5MWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T18:40:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T18:40:59Z"
      },
      "message": "test(app): the start of the program stands after the zero-time opening rapid\n\nPR #2985 (#2901) seats the opening rapid of an operation on its own\nentry X/Y, so it takes no time. At t = 0 `stock_play::progress` counts\nthat segment as complete (cum[0] == 0), and `position_at` gives move 1,\nnot move 0. The step logic is correct; the expectation was stale.\n\nThe test now asserts that the move index equals the count of zero-time\nopening segments of Face1, that these segments are rapids, that the\nstart of Face1 is t = 0, and (unchanged) that the picture is the uncut\nstock. No assert is weaker.\n\nRefs #2608\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
